#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Verify the psbfile function and exception surfaces against the target ELF.

The stripped Android binary still carries one ``.eh_frame`` FDE per emitted
function in both psbfile ranges.  This verifier compares those independent
function boundaries with MANIFEST.md and rejects gaps, overlaps, extra starts,
missing starts, a changed target binary, or a missing adjacent-module boundary.
It also decodes all 39 GCC LSDA call-site tables and compares their 232 entries,
action records, and null catch-all type slots with an explicit expected manifest.
The 150 unique nonzero landing roots are then walked through an independent
AArch64 explicit-control-flow decoder: exception-only cleanup instructions,
successors, calls, terminate/rethrow classes, and normal-flow separation are
hashed as one machine-verifiable landing-pad contract surface.
The complementary entry-rooted normal CFG is decoded with its own narrower
noreturn set, preserving all emitted fallback paths after TVP/TJS diagnostic
helpers.  Together the normal and landing graphs must partition every one of
the 5,525 instructions in the 114 FDEs, while every RET/tail/true-noreturn
terminal is classified against the recovered source-facing return ABI.
Every normal conditional branch is then decoded as a predicate contract:
B.cond condition families and their unique linear NZCV producers, CBZ/CBNZ
width/sense/register fields, and TBZ/TBNZ bit/sense/register fields are fixed
independently from the already-verified successor graph.
Every register input consumed by those CMP/CMN/SUBS producers is then
backwards-sliced to its complete instruction, entry-parameter, or call-return
source set, including loop-carried and packed-width joins.
Every CBZ/CBNZ/TBZ/TBNZ tested register is then backwards-sliced over that CFG
to its complete set of instruction, entry-parameter, or call-return producers;
all join cardinalities, producer words/destinations, and call-clobber boundaries
are fixed by a second canonical manifest.
Every normal W0/X0/D0 value-returning RET is likewise backwards-sliced to its
complete producer set, fixing all success, fallback, diagnostic-continuation,
null, numeric-conversion, and callback-return values independently of the
coarser source-facing return ABI classification.
Every continuing normal BL/BLR is also followed forwards from its fallthrough
to the first physical W0/X0 use, overwrite, later call boundary, or RET on each
finite CFG path.  This complementary surface distinguishes explicit result
consumption from void-result residue and records loops that retain the register
before its first event.
Every normal direct BL and out-of-function B tail transfer is additionally
decoded from the entry-rooted CFG, its complete AAPCS64 register-argument
layout is pinned, and each argument is backwards-sliced to its exact
instruction, entry-parameter, or preceding-call source.  Hidden X8 result
slots, the D0 floating argument, writeback-produced bases, multi-source joins,
and volatile call boundaries are therefore checked independently of call
results and callee bodies.
The inverse consumer surface is scanned independently across the complete ELF
``.text`` section: all 303 direct calls from 25 non-MANIFEST FDEs into 15
psbfile entries are fixed by owner/site/target/word, while two weak-symbol PLT
aliases are proved to be ADRP/LDR/ADD/BR stubs rather than consumer calls.  The
ObjSource adaptor vtable, native/adaptor lifetime FDEs, raw-owner rollback sites
and constructor/destructor helper edges then make that caller census an object-
lifetime contract instead of a bare xref count.
The complementary inverse pointer surface scans every ``.text`` instruction
whose ADRP page can reach a MANIFEST entry, rejects any unlisted ADR, literal
load, or move-wide materialization, and parses every ``.rela.dyn``/``.rela.plt``
entry whose addend or dynamic-symbol value names a MANIFEST function.  This
separates seven module-owned callback/member-pointer pairs, 62 loader/vtable
pointers, two weak-symbol PLT aliases, and one adjacent PackinOne page collision
without treating relocation metadata or shared ncbind base tables as psbfile
consumers.
The cross-module OwnerFilter bridge is then fixed independently from both
directions.  It proves the eager 32-byte TU-static ``std::function`` lifetime,
the separately emitted thin replacement wrapper and copy-assignment FDEs, both
setter target/control-block shapes, all manager op=2/op=3 calls, the unique
Adopt invoker call, and the exact ResourceManager -> LoadStorage -> Adopt
forwarding chain.
The owning emoteplayer registration path is fixed separately as well: one eager
``emoteplayer.dll`` auto-register node points at the sole entry callback, that
entry loads ``motionplayer.dll``, attaches the fully populated EmotePlayer class
to Motion, and injects both decrypt setters into ResourceManager.  The adjacent
motionplayer namespace registrar is pinned to its eleven actual subclass
registration edges and is required not to register EmotePlayer itself.
Finally, it pins every data-referenced psbfile literal, all 42 compiler switch
tables (915 signed relative entries), every switch selector's exact producer,
normalization, unsigned range guard, table-address materialization, and signed
relative dispatch chain, the producer load for every non-switch indirect
transfer, the typed-member instruction surface, and the complete stack-frame/
callee-save/canary surface.  Every instruction-backed typed-member W/RW event
is additionally tied to its selected STR/STP operand and complete normal-CFG
value-producer set, so branch-family, diagnostic, virtual/member-call ABI,
object-field data flow, or local-lifetime drift cannot hide behind unchanged
function boundaries.
The 67 optimizer-synthetic typed-member expressions without individual ctree
addresses are also pinned separately: their exact semantic text/type/offset
records map to 73 nearest emitted machine anchors, including coalesced stores,
direct loads, std::function manager calls, and packed-tag switch dispatches.
Five newly recovered PSBRawOwner/PSBFile typed reads extend that legacy
483-row surface to 488 rows.  Finally, all remaining 667 raw cot_ptr/cot_idx
expressions are fixed by owner-local ordinal, access context, semantic digest,
exact ARM64 word, and entry-rooted normal-CFG realization anchor.
The complementary complete cot_num surface fixes 1,181 source-facing numeric
expressions, including 48 optimizer-synthetic rows, against 1,055 nearest
normal-flow anchors.  Keeping it separate from the raw machine-immediate census
prevents frame, address-materialization and system-register immediates from
being promoted into portable C++ tokens.
The complete Hex-Rays local-variable surface then fixes all 1,056 declarations
and 3,073 cot_var occurrences.  Declaration types, width/location classes,
argument/result/by-reference flags and exact definition anchors remain separate
from use parent/operand topology, syntactic R/W/address mode and 2,214 exact
normal-flow realization anchors.  This catches lvar merge/split, hidden ABI
parameter and local-object drift without treating ARM64 stack/register choices
as portable source layout.
The complementary complete Hex-Rays statement tree fixes all 2,922 cit_*
nodes, their owner-local preorder, parent/child relation, nesting depth, root
expression operator, labels/goto targets, and 1,942 exact normal-flow anchors.
Synthetic blocks, breaks, gotos, returns and expressions remain explicitly
separate from concrete EAs and inherit only their nearest parent anchor.  This
captures decompiler-recovered high-level control topology without pretending
that optimized/inlined loops uniquely recover the original C++ spelling.
The complete Hex-Rays expression tree then fixes all 9,629 cexpr/cot_* nodes,
their direct parent and owning statement, child relation, recovered type,
operator detail, flags, and 3,076 exact normal-flow realization anchors.  Its
statement roots, numeric leaves and local-variable leaves are cross-checked
row-for-row against the independent statement, cot_num and cot_var manifests.
The derived cot_call surface finally separates 405 source-tree calls into
direct, computed-indirect and helper-intrinsic families.  Every real transfer
must match its BL/B/BLR/BR target, while the 200 additional machine-only
transfers remain explicitly attributed to lowering, EH and canary behavior
rather than invented source calls.
The complete cot_obj leaf surface then classifies all 457 recovered object and
address constants by exact ELF section and source context.  Direct callees,
address-taken callbacks, code-range numeric collisions, literal addresses,
vtable address points, initialized pointer objects, BSS subobjects, and the
pthread import pseudo-address form one exhaustive disjoint partition.
The residual leaf surface closes the remaining 118 cot_fnum/cot_empty/cot_helper
nodes.  It fixes all floating constants and source-empty control expressions,
joins the 80 helper callees with their 31 TPIDR_EL0 argument leaves, and proves
that the six leaf operators and 4,800 internal operators partition the complete
9,629-row expression tree without an unclassified node.
The complete cot_memptr/cot_memref surface then fixes all 625 recovered member
expressions, including the 86 nested field-chain bases intentionally omitted by
the earlier outermost-only typed-member projections.  Every node is bound to an
exact normal-flow word, while the 539 outer expressions are cross-checked
against the independent typed read/write/synthetic surfaces and all six chain
shapes are followed to their terminal base.
The complete cot_asg surface next fixes all 1,123 assignment operators and both
of their ordered children.  Its five disjoint destination families are joined
to the lvar, typed-member, raw-memory, global-BSS, and helper-leaf surfaces, so
source assignments, nested address computation, landing-only cleanup stores,
and Hex-Rays LOBYTE/LODWORD pseudo-lvalues remain explicitly distinct.
The exhaustive remainder of the internal expression tree then fixes all 1,980
cast/ref/arithmetic/predicate/mutation/comma nodes.  Address-of and mutation
operands are joined to the lvar, member, raw-memory, and object projections,
while these six families plus the 2,820 dedicated nodes partition all 4,800
internal operators without inferring source semantics from recovered type text.
The direct heap lifecycle is then joined across those existing surfaces: every
allocator result is tied to its argument slice, first result event, normal
publish/transfer/cleanup anchors and constructor-exception cleanup edge.  A
complete census of direct delete/aligned-delete/vector-storage/shared-release
sites keeps normal and landing-only destruction paths distinct.
Finally, the complete reference-count state-machine surface independently pins
all initial values, non-atomic intrusive retain/release triples, optimizer-folded
zero probes, pthread-gated COW decrement fallbacks, shared-string atomic retains,
virtual AddRef/Release ordering sites, direct helper counts, and the external
helper bodies which implement type-specific terminal behavior.
The complete MANIFEST-to-.bss reference census then pins all 94 semantic rows
across 16 targets and 22 owners, including exact ADRP/ADRL materialization,
normal-versus-landing reachability, lazy native-ID publication, AutoRegister
list-head construction order, guarded PSBMedia singleton publication, all
class-info set/clear transitions, and the read-only COW empty representation.
The complementary initialized-data surface pins every semantic .data.rel.ro,
GOT, .data, and extern reference reached from the same 114 FDEs: three missing
base vtables, all 12 consumed Itanium address points, 39 relocation-backed
address-materialization rows, 24 GOT load pairs, five dynamic relocations, and
24 constructor/destructor vptr publication events.
Finally, every apparent code-address data reference is classified.  Ten real
rows materialize seven callbacks/member functions, while fifteen packed
0xFFFFFF masks, two MDF magic constants, and one PSB magic constant are fixed
as numeric address-range collisions rather than invented callable edges.
"""

